.0 |\n| FFO-6—Customs and Border Protection Collection of Duties, Taxes, and Fees by Districts and Ports | 23.0 |\n| ACCOUNT OF THE U.S. TREASURY | nan |\n| Introduction—Source and Availability of the Balance in the Account of the U.S. Treasury | 29.0 |\n| UST-1—Elements of Change in Federal Reserve and Tax and Loan Note Account Balances | 29.0 |\n| FEDERAL DEBT | nan |\n| Introduction—Federal Debt | 31.0 |\n| FD-1—Summary of Federal Debt | 32.0 |\n| FD-2—Debt Held by the Public | 33.0 |\n| FD-3—Government Account Series | 34.0 |\n| FD-4—Interest-Bearing Securities Issued by Government Agencies | 35.0 |\n| FD-5—Maturity Distribution and Average Length of Marketable Interest-Bearing Public Debt Held by Private Investors | 36.0 |\n| FD-6—Debt Subject to Statutory Limit | 37.0 |\n=== /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2016_12_page_21.txt ===\n16\nFEDERAL FISCAL OPERATIONS\nTABLE FFO-3—On-Budget and Off-Budget Outlays by Agency\n[In millions of dollars. Source: \"Monthly Treasury Statement of Receipts and Outlays of the United States Government\"]\n<table><tr><th>Fiscal year or month</th><th>Legislative branch (1)</th><th>Judicial branch (2)</th><th>Department of Agriculture (3)</th><th>Department of Commerce (4)</th><th>Department of Defense, military (5)</th><th>Department of Education (6)</th><th>Department of Energy (7)</th><th>Department of Health and Human Services (8)</th><th>Department of Homeland Security (9)</th><th>Department of Housing and Urban Development (10)</th><th>Department of the Interior (11)</th><th>Department of Justice (12)</th><th>Department of Labor (13)</th></tr><tr><td>2012</td><td>4,438</td><td>7,228</td><td>139,712</td><td>10,267</td><td>650,869</td><td>57,248</td><td>32,485</td><td>848,055</td><td>47,423</td><td>49,591</td><td>12,886</td><td>31,161</td><td>104,742</td></tr><tr><td>2013</td><td>4,328</td><td>7,066</td><td>155,897</td><td>9,137</td><td>607,801</td><td>40,910</td><td>24,677</td><td>886,293</td><td>57,220</td><td>56,577</td><td>